{"availability":"available","full":"Basekick-Labs/arc","name":"arc","description":"Open, SQL-native time-series database for telemetry you need to keep. 34M+ records/sec ingestion, 8M+ rows/sec queries. InfluxDB Line Protocol and Telegraf compatible. Open Parquet on your storage. Single binary. S3/Azure native. Air-gap ready. AGPL-3.0.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":680,"forks":56,"created":"2025-10-07T15:27:59Z","updated":"2026-10-07T23:13:01Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://basekick.net","topics":["ai","analytical-database","analytics","columnar-database","data-warehouse","database","edge-computing","events","high-performance","iot","logs","observability","olap","parquet","performance","s3","time-series","traces"],"demo":"https://basekick.net/demos","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:30:40.860Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:30:40.860Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:30:40.860Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:50.104Z","stars":679,"forks":56},{"at":"2026-10-07T23:30:40.860Z","stars":680,"forks":56}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Machines, services, vehicles, and devices produce data continuously. The operational problem is not only ingesting the latest readings — it is keeping the full-resolution history available for debugging, analysis, compliance, and the next question nobody has asked yet.","Teams evaluating a time-series database usually run into the same trade-offs:","Arc is built for teams that want to keep the data, query the whole history, and start with a small deployment. It combines high-throughput ingestion, automatic Parquet storage and compaction, analytical SQL, retention policies, and continuous queries in one binary."],"features":["Retention cliffs: Older data is downsampled, exported, or deleted because storage costs grow too quickly.","Split hot and cold paths: Recent data is queryable in one system while historical data waits in a warehouse or object store.","Operational overhead: A simple workload turns into a PostgreSQL extension stack or a multi-service cluster.","Migration friction: Existing agents, dashboards, and Line Protocol writers make changing databases risky.","Vendor lock-in: Proprietary storage makes it difficult to use your data elsewhere or leave later."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Basekick-Labs/arc/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"076f4c66e271c540c37ce3d63bc5281abfc77a8f5f5ab24066f23c3284f02ebc","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:31:16.239Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:31:16.239Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Machines, services, vehicles, and devices produce data continuously. The operational problem is not only ingesting the latest readings — it is keeping the full-resolution history available for debugging, analysis, compliance, and the next question nobody has asked yet.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Basekick-Labs/arc/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Arc is built for teams that want to keep the data, query the whole history, and start with a small deployment. It combines high-throughput ingestion, automatic Parquet storage and compaction, analytical SQL, retention policies, and continuous queries in one binary.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Basekick-Labs/arc/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Arc Launchpad is a self-hosted web console for the Arc instances you run — SQL console, schema explorer, logs, monitoring, and management for tokens, retention, alerts, continuous queries, and MQTT ingestion.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Basekick-Labs/arc/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"076f4c66e271c540c37ce3d63bc5281abfc77a8f5f5ab24066f23c3284f02ebc","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Basekick-Labs/arc/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T00:31:16.240Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T23:13:01Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourc